From: CEB-GNRD maintainers <bmc@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: block software start and reset during host flash programming

Use a backend lock shared by all Host/Chassis transition setters.
BIOS/CPLD acquire it before waiting for stable Off. Shutdown remains
available; On, reboot/cycle and force-button pulses are refused until
the programmer releases the lock. A read-only board property excludes
power-on/cycle wait states that the generic Chassis API calls Off.
The BIOS updater releases its lock only
after unbinding MTD and returning flash ownership, before its power cycle.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CEB-GNRD update policy]

diff --git a/src/power_control.cpp b/src/power_control.cpp
--- a/src/power_control.cpp
